        "problem": "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}=1?$",
        "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{1}=1$ and $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t.\n$$",
